From 19a56c4fd954e67431d6858d9de20467d984bde0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ferdinand Vanmaele <ferdinand-joseph.vanmaele@uni-a.de>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:56:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] [clangd] workspace/symbol: mid-word matches on request
 (middleMatch)

A client may send middleMatch: N with workspace/symbol.  Then, for a
query of at least N characters (3 or more), a symbol whose identifier
contains the query in any case matches too ("ector" finds
"TangentVector"), which FuzzyMatcher refuses because the query does not
start a word segment.  Template arguments are not searched: a class
template's constructor is named "Holder<VectorType>".  Such matches
score below zero in Dex and MemIndex and below every fuzzy match in
getWorkspaceSymbols, so they rank last and go first at a limit; the
index's quality factor multiplies the score, so a small positive score
was not enough.  The request field FuzzyFindRequest::MiddleMatch is set
by workspace symbols only; code completion leaves it 0.  The initialize
reply announces workspaceSymbolMatchesProvider.middleMatch.
